{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01392",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.55,
      "end_seconds": 7.52,
      "duration_seconds": 6.97,
      "text": "Doctor, you know, hi, where would you like me to put my coat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.52,
      "end_seconds": 13.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.48,
      "end_seconds": 23.99,
      "duration_seconds": 8.51,
      "text": "Mainly crushing chest pain. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.06,
      "end_seconds": 28.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.81,
      "end_seconds": 36.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "For two months, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.21,
      "end_seconds": 47.26,
      "duration_seconds": 10.05,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.99,
      "end_seconds": 52.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "It happens on and off. I'd call it mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.52,
      "end_seconds": 55.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.4,
      "end_seconds": 82.77,
      "duration_seconds": 25.37,
      "text": "Pain going into my left arm goes along with it, most of the time. The pain going into my left arm? That's been for about a week. With pain going into my left arm, I'd call it mild. It happens once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.05,
      "end_seconds": 101.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any leg swelling, cough or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.03,
      "end_seconds": 108.07,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "Okay, so I haven't had leg swelling, cough or fever, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.15,
      "end_seconds": 113.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "Any change in your bowel habit or your stomach generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.57,
      "end_seconds": 118.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Well, no, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.59,
      "end_seconds": 123.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.13,
      "end_seconds": 126.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "I move fine otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.52,
      "end_seconds": 130.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.47,
      "end_seconds": 134.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "My brother has epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.86,
      "end_seconds": 137.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.96,
      "end_seconds": 141.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.02,
      "end_seconds": 145.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Do you do any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.53,
      "end_seconds": 148.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.35,
      "end_seconds": 154.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.64,
      "end_seconds": 159.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "I don't think I have any, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.1,
      "end_seconds": 173.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.18,
      "end_seconds": 182.57,
      "duration_seconds": 8.39,
      "text": "High cholesterol, for about a year. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.87,
      "end_seconds": 186.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Right, what's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.41,
      "end_seconds": 193.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "I'm on rosuvastatin, 10 milligrams, at night for my cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.57,
      "end_seconds": 196.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.67,
      "end_seconds": 202.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Just a wisdom tooth extraction under sedation, five years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.68,
      "end_seconds": 215.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.01,
      "end_seconds": 229.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.39,
      "end_seconds": 246.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "Okay: respiratory rate 16, temperature 37.1, pulse 106, blood pressure 115 over 72."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.41,
      "end_seconds": 252.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.19,
      "end_seconds": 266.13,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.41,
      "end_seconds": 268.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.29,
      "end_seconds": 284.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "You are pale and sweaty, and your pulse is fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.27,
      "end_seconds": 297.2,
      "duration_seconds": 9.93,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again. Let me tell you where I've got to. My working impression is a possible heart attack."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.05,
      "end_seconds": 302.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.36,
      "end_seconds": 317.57,
      "duration_seconds": 14.21,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a possible heart attack is my leading thought, not anything worse. I think an ECG makes sense here, for chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 319.24,
      "end_seconds": 322.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Where would I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.45,
      "end_seconds": 353.6,
      "duration_seconds": 30.15,
      "text": "For this, aspirin, 300 milligrams, once now, single dose. That's for possible heart attack. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Stay lying down and do not eat or drink. We'll refer you to the cardiac team. If the pain returns, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. Let's review you straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 354.5,
      "end_seconds": 358.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "I'll book it on my way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.93,
      "end_seconds": 364.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "How would you describe the plan, so we're on the same page?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.12,
      "end_seconds": 373.73,
      "duration_seconds": 8.61,
      "text": "So, I take the aspirin, 300 milligrams, once now and come back straight away. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.87,
      "end_seconds": 378.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 379.6,
      "end_seconds": 382.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}